way","description":"With the fantasy trade deadline approaching, here are the players managers should be targeting and ones they can offload.","published":"2026-11-23T23:32:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50574503/2026-fantasy-football-trade-deadline-trade-away","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Commanders RB Jacory Croskey-Merritt activated from IR ahead of MNF","description":"The Commanders activated running back Jacory Croskey-Merritt off injured reserve Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T23:48:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50576561/commanders-rb-jacory-croskey-merritt-activated-ir","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"John Keim","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy buzz: Who got the ball Sunday? Usage trends and role changes","description":"A closer look at the top 10 fantasy scorers in Week 11, including Cowboys QB Dak Prescott and Broncos RB Jonah Coleman.","published":"2026-11-23T21:24:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Fantasy","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Giants' Greg Newsome out 'multiple weeks' with ankle sprain","description":"Giants starting cornerback Greg Newsome will miss \"multiple weeks\" with a high ankle sprain, coach John Harbaugh said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T21:59:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50576454/giants-greg-newsome-multiple-weeks-ankle-sprain","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jordan Raanan","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cardinals fire DC Nick Rallis; Teryl Austin takes over on interim basis","description":"The Cardinals have fired defensive coordinator Nick Rallis, coach Mike LaFleur announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T22:57:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575938/cardinals-fire-defensive-coordinator-nick-rallis-sources-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Josh Weinfuss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rams TE Terrance Ferguson needs season-ending ankle surgery, Sean McVay says","description":"Rams tight end Terrance Ferguson's ankle injury will require season-ending surgery.","published":"2026-11-23T20:41:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575889/rams-te-terrance-ferguson-needs-season-ending-ankle-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Sarah Barshop","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Jacob Saylors","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Saylors","description":"American football player (born 2000)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Jacob Saylors (born March 8, 2000) is an American professional football kick returner and running back for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the East Tennessee State Buccaneers and was signed by the Cincinnati Bengals as an undrafted free agent following the 2023 NFL Draft. With the St. Louis Battlehawks, Saylors was named to the All-UFL team in 2024 and 2025.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Saylors played college football at East Tennessee State, where he rushed for 3,861 yards, and 33 touchdowns.\n\nSTATISTICS"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"CINCINNATI BENGALS\nAfter going undrafted in the 2023 NFL draft, Saylors signed with the Cincinnati Bengals on April 30, 2023. He was waived by the Bengals on August 29.\n\nATLANTA FALCONS\nOn October 18, 2023, Saylors was signed to the Atlanta Falcons' practice squad. He was waived on January 2, 2024, with an injury settlement.\n\nST. LOUIS BATTLEHAWKS (FIRST STINT)\nOn February 5, 2024, Saylors signed with the St. Louis Battlehawks of the United Football League (UFL). He led the league in rushing yards, and was named to the All-UFL team.\n\nNEW YORK GIANTS\nOn June 18, 2024. Saylors signed with the New York Giants. He was waived by the Giants on August 12.\n\nCLEVELAND BROWNS\nOn August 22, 2024, Saylors signed with the Cleveland Browns, but was waived later that week.\n\nST. LOUIS BATTLEHAWKS (SECOND STINT)\nOn November 5, 2024, Saylors re-signed with the Battlehawks.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn July 29, 2025, Saylors signed with the Detroit Lions. He was waived on August 26 as part of final roster cuts, and re-signed to the practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on September 6. In his first NFL regular season game, Saylors primarily played as a return specialist, returning four kickoffs for a total of 92 yards.\nOn January 5, 2026, the Lions signed Saylors to a one-year contract extension."}],"wikidataId":"Q134625884","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-01-05","text":"Signed OLs Devin Cochran and Mason Miller, WRs Malik Cunningham and Jackson Meeks, DE Ahmed Hassanein, TE Zach Horton, RB Jabari Small, DL Chris Smith and S Loren Strickland to reserve/futures contracts. Re-signed OL Michael Niese, RB Jacob Saylors and CB Nick Whiteside."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4383429","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/S/SaylJa00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/jacob-saylors/87559","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/jacob-saylors/11476","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Saylors"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.0M is the 45th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2023 as an undrafted free agent."]}